## Overview of the request flow

`POST /api/owners` → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` → `OwnerMapper.toOwner(...)` → `ClinicService.saveOwner(Owner)` → `OwnerRepository.save(...)`. Bean Validation runs on the DTO before the controller body; the business-rule checks (telephone uniqueness, household duplication) and normalization happen inside `saveOwner`. There are **no JPA lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate`) anywhere — normalization is done manually in the service.

Note there is a V2 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) but it only implements `GET /api/owners` paging (`listOwnersPage`); it does not handle POST. The POST is handled solely by V1.

